  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Software Deployment Tools — SCCM Presence Detection via WMI", "technique": "T1072", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13 09:02:11 CEST, SCCM-SRV-P01 (10.108.57.50) recorded Sysmon Event 1 showing wmiprvse.exe spawning a WMI query targeting the root\\sms namespace from a remote host ATTK-WS-184 (10.108.57.184). The query probed the SMS_Site class to discover SCCM site code P01 and server role. WMI-based SCCM discovery from a non-management host is anomalous and constitutes Phase 1 of software-deployment-tool abuse.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 92790 'WMI SCCM package creation attempt' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1072 and level=13. Sysmon Event 1: data.win.eventdata.image=C:\\Windows\\System32\\wbem\\WmiPrvSE.exe, data.win.eventdata.commandLine contains 'root\\sms' and 'SMS_Site', agent.name=SCCM-SRV-P01.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:02:11+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Software Deployment Tools — SMS_Package WMI Creation Attempt", "technique": "T1072", "what_happened": "At 09:03:47 CEST, the same WMI session from ATTK-WS-184 attempted to instantiate an SMS_Package object in the root\\sms\\site_P01 namespace with PackageName='SCCMDeploy_20260513_090347' and SourcePath pointing to a UNC share on ATTK-WS-184. The WMI provider generated an event even though the operation failed due to insufficient SCCM Admin permissions. Wazuh rule 92790 correlated the failed WMI write as a package-creation attempt — intent is confirmed regardless of outcome.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 19 (WMI event filter created) followed by Sysmon Event 1: wmiprvse.exe + commandLine containing 'SMS_Package' + 'root\\sms\\site_P01'. Rule 92790 level=13. The UNC SourcePath \\\\10.108.57.184\\SCCMShare is the attacker-controlled staging path for malicious payload delivery.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:03:47+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Software Deployment Tools — CCM Client Deployment Catalog Enumeration", "technique": "T1072", "what_happened": "At 09:05:22 CEST, ATTK-WS-184 queried the local CCM client SDK on SCCM-SRV-P01 using CcmExec.exe to enumerate deployed packages and target collections. The CCM client RPC call returned the full deployment catalog including package IDs, assigned collection GUIDs, and deployment schedules — giving the attacker a blueprint of all managed systems reachable via SCCM. Wazuh rule 92791 'SCCM catalog enumeration' (level=12) fired with T1072.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1: data.win.eventdata.image=C:\\Windows\\CCM\\CcmExec.exe + commandLine targeting WMI root\\ccm\\clientsdk namespace + data.win.eventdata.user=CORP\\jsmith. rule.id=92791 rule.level=12 rule.mitre.id=T1072. The account CORP\\jsmith is a regular domain user — NOT an SCCM administrator — confirming unauthorized enumeration.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:05:22+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Software Deployment Tools — Malicious Script Stub Drop (FIM)", "technique": "T1072", "what_happened": "At 09:07:55 CEST, Wazuh FIM detected file creation under C:\\Windows\\Temp\\SCCMDeploy_20260513_090347\\ on SCCM-SRV-P01. The directory name matches the PackageName from Step 2 exactly. Files dropped include deploy.cmd (batch launcher), payload.ps1 (PowerShell stub), and sccm_stub.xml (deployment descriptor). These artefacts form a complete SCCM package structure intended for mass deployment to all managed endpoints if the package-creation WMI call had succeeded — or for manual import by an insider with SCCM access.", "chain_reason": "syscheck.path=C:\\Windows\\Temp\\SCCMDeploy_20260513_090347\\payload.ps1 syscheck.event=added agent.name=SCCM-SRV-P01. The directory timestamp 090347 matches the package creation attempt at 09:03:47 exactly. Three files (deploy.cmd, payload.ps1, sccm_stub.xml) confirm a fully prepared SCCM package payload.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:07:55+0200"}
  ],
